INSERT INTO `candidates` VALUES ('app_0a7d481d',18,'Test 5',NULL,NULL,'1_STRONG_HIRE_Elena_Voss.pdf','Elena Voss\nSenior Backend Engineer (Python)\nSingapore, SG  | +65 5588 2201  | elena.voss@fictionalmail.com  | linkedin.com/in/elenavoss-demo\nSUMMARY\nSenior backend engineer with 8 years building and scaling Python services for high-traffic platforms. Deep hands-on\nexpertise across the full stack requested for this role: FastAPI/Django, PostgreSQL, Redis, Kafka, containerized\ndeployments on AWS with Kubernetes, and mature CI/CD practice. Regularly leads architecture decisions and\nmentors junior engineers.\nSKILLS\nPython (8 yrs)  | FastAPI  | Django REST Framework  | PostgreSQL  | Redis  | Kafka  | RabbitMQ  | AWS (EKS,\nRDS, ElastiCache)  | Docker  | Kubernetes  | CI/CD (GitHub Actions, ArgoCD)  | System Architecture  | Mentoring &\nCode Review\nEXPERIENCE\nSenior Backend Engineer — Northfield Data Systems\nSingapore  | Jun 2020 – Present\n Designed and led migration of a monolithic Django app to FastAPI microservices on Kubernetes (EKS), cutting p95\nlatency by 46%.\n Built the event-streaming layer on Kafka handling 40M+ events/day, replacing a brittle polling system.\n Own the CI/CD pipeline (GitHub Actions ® ArgoCD) used by all 6 backend squads; deploys went from weekly to\nmultiple times daily.\n Mentor 3 junior engineers; run the team\'s architecture review sessions.\nBackend Engineer — Ridgeline Software\nSingapore  | Jul 2017 – May 2020\n Built REST APIs in Django REST Framework backed by PostgreSQL and Redis caching, serving 2M+ daily active\nusers.\n Containerized all services with Docker; introduced RabbitMQ for async job processing.\nSoftware Engineer — Cobalt Applications\nKuala Lumpur, MY  | Aug 2015 – Jun 2017\n Developed Python data-processing pipelines and internal tooling for a 20-person engineering team.\nEDUCATION\nB.Sc. in Computer Science — National University of Singapore, 2015\nCERTIFICATIONS\nAWS Certified Solutions Architect – Associate, Certified Kubernetes Application Developer (CKAD)','Elena Voss\nSenior Backend Engineer (Python)\nSingapore, SG  | +65 5588 2201  | [REDACTED EMAIL]  | linkedin.com/in/elenavoss-demo\nSUMMARY\nSenior backend engineer with 8 years building and scaling Python services for high-traffic platforms. Deep hands-on\nexpertise across the full stack requested for this role: FastAPI/Django, PostgreSQL, Redis, Kafka, containerized\ndeployments on AWS with Kubernetes, and mature CI/CD practice. Regularly leads architecture decisions and\nmentors junior engineers.\nSKILLS\nPython (8 yrs)  | FastAPI  | Django REST Framework  | PostgreSQL  | Redis  | Kafka  | RabbitMQ  | AWS (EKS,\nRDS, ElastiCache)  | Docker  | Kubernetes  | CI/CD (GitHub Actions, ArgoCD)  | System Architecture  | Mentoring &\nCode Review\nEXPERIENCE\nSenior Backend Engineer — Northfield Data Systems\nSingapore  | Jun 2020 – Present\n Designed and led migration of a monolithic Django app to FastAPI microservices on Kubernetes (EKS), cutting p95\nlatency by 46%.\n Built the event-streaming layer on Kafka handling 40M+ events/day, replacing a brittle polling system.\n Own the CI/CD pipeline (GitHub Actions ® ArgoCD) used by all 6 backend squads; deploys went from weekly to\nmultiple times daily.\n Mentor 3 junior engineers; run the team\'s architecture review sessions.\nBackend Engineer — Ridgeline Software\nSingapore  | Jul 2017 – May 2020\n Built REST APIs in Django REST Framework backed by PostgreSQL and Redis caching, serving 2M+ daily active\nusers.\n Containerized all services with Docker; introduced RabbitMQ for async job processing.\nSoftware Engineer — Cobalt Applications\nKuala Lumpur, MY  | Aug 2015 – Jun 2017\n Developed Python data-processing pipelines and internal tooling for a 20-person engineering team.\nEDUCATION\nB.Sc. in Computer Science — National University of Singapore, 2015\nCERTIFICATIONS\nAWS Certified Solutions Architect – Associate, Certified Kubernetes Application Developer (CKAD)','Review','Strong Hire',91,98,80,88,'ATS Evaluation against Job Description requirements: Fulfills 100% of core required technical qualifications (Python, AWS, Docker). Solid overall alignment with position expectations.','Tertiary Education / Diploma','3+ Years Relevant Experience','[\"Python\",\"AWS\",\"Docker\"]','[\"Directly matches mandatory Job Description skills: Python, AWS, Docker [Resume Evidence: \\\"Singapore, SG  | +65 5588 2201  | [REDACTED EMAIL]  | linkedin.com\\/in\\/elenavoss-demo\\\"].\",\"Documented background in relevant functional deliverables matching role requirements [Resume Evidence: \\\"deployments on AWS with Kubernetes, and mature CI\\/CD practice. Regularly leads architecture decisions and\\\"].\"]','[\"Recommend verifying practical depth of experience in high-scale production scenarios [Resume Evidence: Resume lists key skills but lacks metric-driven production impact stats].\"]','Strong Hire','ATS Screener Note: Candidate brings strong alignment with core required deliverables.','1. Can you walk us through a recent project where you delivered key requirements matching this job description?\n2. How do your past accomplishments specifically prepare you for the main duties outlined in this job description?',1,'2026-08-20 08:27:55',20,'uploads/6a86ba88f0d4e_1_STRONG_HIRE_Elena_Voss.pdf','https://www.youtube.com/',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-08-20 08:27:55','None',NULL,NULL,NULL),('app_1213c798',18,'Test 3',NULL,NULL,'03_Diego_Farrow_VP_Engineering.pdf','Diego Farrow\nVP of Engineering\nAustin, TX, US  | +1 (512) 555-0148  | diego.farrow@fictionalmail.com  | linkedin.com/in/diegofarrow-demo\nEXECUTIVE SUMMARY\nEngineering executive focused on e-commerce and marketplace platforms at scale. Track record building high-velocity\nproduct engineering teams, improving checkout conversion through performance engineering, and mentoring first-time\nmanagers into senior leaders.\nCORE COMPETENCIES\nMarketplace & E-Commerce Platforms  | Team Scaling (0®150 engineers)  | Performance Engineering  | A/B Testing\n& Experimentation  | React/Node.js Architecture  | Engineering Career Frameworks  | Cross-functional Product\nPartnership\nPROFESSIONAL EXPERIENCE\nVP of Engineering — Cartwheel Marketplace Inc.\nAustin, TX  | Apr 2020 – Present\n Grew engineering org from 35 to 150 across checkout, search, and seller-tools pillars ahead of a Series D raise.\n Led site-wide performance initiative that reduced median page load time by 55%, lifting checkout conversion 8.4%.\n Built an internal engineering leadership program that promoted 14 engineers into management in 3 years.\nSenior Director of Engineering — Palette Retail Technologies\nDenver, CO  | Jan 2016 – Mar 2020\n Owned platform powering USD 900M in annual GMV across web and mobile.\n Introduced feature-flagging and progressive rollout system, cutting production incident rate by 37%.\nEngineering Manager — Hearthstone Goods Co.\nChicago, IL  | Aug 2011 – Dec 2015\n Led 12-engineer team rebuilding the catalog and pricing engine, supporting 3x SKU growth.\nEDUCATION\nB.S. in Computer Engineering — University of Texas at Austin, 2011\nCERTIFICATIONS\nCertified Scrum Product Owner (CSPO), AWS Certified DevOps Engineer','Diego Farrow\nVP of Engineering\nAustin, TX, US  | +1 (512) 555-0148  | [REDACTED EMAIL]  | linkedin.com/in/diegofarrow-demo\nEXECUTIVE SUMMARY\nEngineering executive focused on e-commerce and marketplace platforms at scale. Track record building high-velocity\nproduct engineering teams, improving checkout conversion through performance engineering, and mentoring first-time\nmanagers into senior leaders.\nCORE COMPETENCIES\nMarketplace & E-Commerce Platforms  | Team Scaling (0®150 engineers)  | Performance Engineering  | A/B Testing\n& Experimentation  | React/Node.js Architecture  | Engineering Career Frameworks  | Cross-functional Product\nPartnership\nPROFESSIONAL EXPERIENCE\nVP of Engineering — Cartwheel Marketplace Inc.\nAustin, TX  | Apr 2020 – Present\n Grew engineering org from 35 to 150 across checkout, search, and seller-tools pillars ahead of a Series D raise.\n Led site-wide performance initiative that reduced median page load time by 55%, lifting checkout conversion 8.4%.\n Built an internal engineering leadership program that promoted 14 engineers into management in 3 years.\nSenior Director of Engineering — Palette Retail Technologies\nDenver, CO  | Jan 2016 – Mar 2020\n Owned platform powering USD 900M in annual GMV across web and mobile.\n Introduced feature-flagging and progressive rollout system, cutting production incident rate by 37%.\nEngineering Manager — Hearthstone Goods Co.\nChicago, IL  | Aug 2011 – Dec 2015\n Led 12-engineer team rebuilding the catalog and pricing engine, supporting 3x SKU growth.\nEDUCATION\nB.S. in Computer Engineering — University of Texas at Austin, 2011\nCERTIFICATIONS\nCertified Scrum Product Owner (CSPO), AWS Certified DevOps Engineer','Review','Maybe',58,33,80,88,'ATS Evaluation against Job Description requirements: Fulfills 33% of core required technical qualifications (AWS). Gaps noted for Python, Docker.','Tertiary Education / Diploma','3+ Years Relevant Experience','[\"AWS\"]','[\"Directly matches mandatory Job Description skills: AWS [Resume Evidence: \\\"Austin, TX, US  | +1 (512) 555-0148  | [REDACTED EMAIL]  | linkedin.com\\/in\\/diegofarrow-demo\\\"].\",\"Documented background in relevant functional deliverables matching role requirements [Resume Evidence: \\\"EXECUTIVE SUMMARY\\\"].\"]','[\"Missing explicit documented experience for required Job Description skill(s): Python, Docker [Resume Evidence: Candidate resume contains 0 mentions of Python or Docker].\"]','Maybe','ATS Screener Note: Candidate brings partial alignment with key JD skills that require targeted technical interview probing.','1. The job description requires experience with Python. Can you detail your actual working knowledge or equivalent experience with this requirement?\n2. How do your past accomplishments specifically prepare you for the main duties outlined in this job description?',1,'2026-08-20 08:14:07',18,'uploads/6a86b74e54480_03_Diego_Farrow_VP_Engineering.pdf','https://www.youtube.com/',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-08-20 08:14:07','None',NULL,NULL,NULL),('app_5333640d',20,'Test 9',NULL,NULL,'4_DO_NOT_HIRE_Kevin_Lim_field_mismatch.pdf','Kevin Lim Wei Jian\nJunior Graphic Designer\nPenang, MY  | +60 16 552 3390  | kevin.lim@fictionalmail.com  | linkedin.com/in/kevinlim-demo\nSUMMARY\nJunior graphic designer with 3 years of experience creating marketing visuals, packaging artwork, and social media\ngraphics for a consumer products company. No experience in human resources, recruitment, payroll, or office\nadministration.\nSKILLS\nAdobe Photoshop  | Adobe Illustrator  | Figma  | Packaging Design  | Social Media Graphics  | Brand Visual Identity  | \nPrint Production Coordination\nEXPERIENCE\nJunior Graphic Designer — Warna Kreatif Studio\nGeorgetown, Penang  | Apr 2022 – Present\n Design packaging artwork and marketing collateral for consumer product clients.\n Create social media graphics and short animated ads for client campaigns.\nDesign Intern — Pixel Bay Advertising\nGeorgetown, Penang  | Jan 2021 – Mar 2022\n Supported senior designers on print production files and client mockups.\nEDUCATION\nDiploma in Graphic Design — Dasein Academy of Art, 2021','Kevin Lim Wei Jian\nJunior Graphic Designer\nPenang, MY  | +60 16 552 3390  | [REDACTED EMAIL]  | linkedin.com/in/kevinlim-demo\nSUMMARY\nJunior graphic designer with 3 years of experience creating marketing visuals, packaging artwork, and social media\ngraphics for a consumer products company. No experience in human resources, recruitment, payroll, or office\nadministration.\nSKILLS\nAdobe Photoshop  | Adobe Illustrator  | Figma  | Packaging Design  | Social Media Graphics  | Brand Visual Identity  | \nPrint Production Coordination\nEXPERIENCE\nJunior Graphic Designer — Warna Kreatif Studio\nGeorgetown, Penang  | Apr 2022 – Present\n Design packaging artwork and marketing collateral for consumer product clients.\n Create social media graphics and short animated ads for client campaigns.\nDesign Intern — Pixel Bay Advertising\nGeorgetown, Penang  | Jan 2021 – Mar 2022\n Supported senior designers on print production files and client mockups.\nEDUCATION\nDiploma in Graphic Design — Dasein Academy of Art, 2021','Review','Do Not Hire',24,10,20,65,'ATS Evaluation against Job Description requirements: Fulfills 0% of core required technical qualifications (). Gaps noted for Management, Communication.','Tertiary Education / Diploma','3+ Years Relevant Experience','[\"Problem Solving\",\"Teamwork\"]','[\"Strong, detailed professional background relevant to the role.\",\"Experience coordinating teams or managing responsibilities shows some leadership potential.\"]','[\"No documented experience with Management.\",\"No documented experience with Communication.\"]','Do Not Hire','ATS Screener Note: Candidate brings partial alignment with key JD skills that require targeted technical interview probing.','1. The job description requires experience with Management. Can you detail your actual working knowledge or equivalent experience with this requirement?\n2. How do your past accomplishments specifically prepare you for the main duties outlined in this job description?',1,'2026-08-21 02:05:38',36,'uploads/6a87b2708680f_4_DO_NOT_HIRE_Kevin_Lim_field_mismatch.pdf','https://www.youtube.com/',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-08-21 02:15:28','None',NULL,NULL,NULL),('app_5b5f9511',21,'testing',NULL,NULL,'1_STRONG_HIRE_Aisyah_Rahman.pdf','Aisyah Rahman\nHR Executive\nPetaling Jaya, Selangor, MY  | +60 12 345 6721  | aisyah.rahman@fictionalmail.com  | \nlinkedin.com/in/aisyahrahman-demo\nSUMMARY\nHR Executive with 4 years of hands-on experience supporting the full employee lifecycle for a mid-sized services\ncompany in Malaysia. Comfortable managing recruitment coordination, onboarding, training logistics, HR records,\npayroll administration support, and employee relations with discretion and professionalism. Solid working knowledge\nof the Malaysian Employment Act 1955 and PDPA requirements.\nSKILLS\nFull Employee Lifecycle Administration  | Recruitment Coordination & Preliminary Interviews  | Onboarding &\nOffboarding  | Training & Development Coordination  | HR Records & PDPA Compliance  | Payroll Administration\nSupport  | Malaysian Employment Law  | HRMS (BrioHR)  | Microsoft Office (Excel, Word, PowerPoint)  | Employee\nRelations  | Event & Engagement Coordination\nEXPERIENCE\nHR Executive — Cempaka Business Solutions Sdn. Bhd.\nPetaling Jaya, Selangor  | Mar 2021 – Present\n Support the full employee lifecycle for a 180-staff organisation, including recruitment, onboarding, training\ncoordination, and offboarding.\n Draft job descriptions and job postings, and conduct preliminary phone/in-person interviews before shortlisting\ncandidates to hiring managers.\n Maintain employee records in BrioHR and ensure filing practices comply with PDPA requirements.\n Coordinate monthly training sessions and quarterly team-building/engagement events for the company.\n Assist the Finance team with payroll administration, verifying attendance, leave, and claims data each month for\n180 employees.\n Handle day-to-day employee queries on leave, benefits, and HR policy with empathy and confidentiality.\n Support HR compliance reviews to ensure adherence to the Employment Act 1955 and related regulations.\nHR Assistant — Melur Retail Group\nShah Alam, Selangor  | Jan 2019 – Feb 2021\n Provided administrative support to a 3-person HR team, including maintaining HR databases and physical filing\nsystems.\n Assisted with recruitment logistics — scheduling interviews, preparing offer letters, and coordinating new-hire\npaperwork.\nEDUCATION\nDiploma in Human Resource Management — Universiti Teknologi MARA (UiTM), 2018\nSijil Pelajaran Malaysia (SPM) — SMK Bukit Bintang, 2015\nCERTIFICATIONS\nCIPD Level 3 Foundation Certificate in People Practice','Aisyah Rahman\nHR Executive\nPetaling Jaya, Selangor, MY  | +60 12 345 6721  | [REDACTED EMAIL]  | \nlinkedin.com/in/aisyahrahman-demo\nSUMMARY\nHR Executive with 4 years of hands-on experience supporting the full employee lifecycle for a mid-sized services\ncompany in Malaysia. Comfortable managing recruitment coordination, onboarding, training logistics, HR records,\npayroll administration support, and employee relations with discretion and professionalism. Solid working knowledge\nof the Malaysian Employment Act 1955 and PDPA requirements.\nSKILLS\nFull Employee Lifecycle Administration  | Recruitment Coordination & Preliminary Interviews  | Onboarding &\nOffboarding  | Training & Development Coordination  | HR Records & PDPA Compliance  | Payroll Administration\nSupport  | Malaysian Employment Law  | HRMS (BrioHR)  | Microsoft Office (Excel, Word, PowerPoint)  | Employee\nRelations  | Event & Engagement Coordination\nEXPERIENCE\nHR Executive — Cempaka Business Solutions Sdn. Bhd.\nPetaling Jaya, Selangor  | Mar 2021 – Present\n Support the full employee lifecycle for a 180-staff organisation, including recruitment, onboarding, training\ncoordination, and offboarding.\n Draft job descriptions and job postings, and conduct preliminary phone/in-person interviews before shortlisting\ncandidates to hiring managers.\n Maintain employee records in BrioHR and ensure filing practices comply with PDPA requirements.\n Coordinate monthly training sessions and quarterly team-building/engagement events for the company.\n Assist the Finance team with payroll administration, verifying attendance, leave, and claims data each month for\n180 employees.\n Handle day-to-day employee queries on leave, benefits, and HR policy with empathy and confidentiality.\n Support HR compliance reviews to ensure adherence to the Employment Act 1955 and related regulations.\nHR Assistant — Melur Retail Group\nShah Alam, Selangor  | Jan 2019 – Feb 2021\n Provided administrative support to a 3-person HR team, including maintaining HR databases and physical filing\nsystems.\n Assisted with recruitment logistics — scheduling interviews, preparing offer letters, and coordinating new-hire\npaperwork.\nEDUCATION\nDiploma in Human Resource Management — Universiti Teknologi MARA (UiTM), 2018\nSijil Pelajaran Malaysia (SPM) — SMK Bukit Bintang, 2015\nCERTIFICATIONS\nCIPD Level 3 Foundation Certificate in People Practice','Review','Hire',78,75,80,80,'The uploaded file is a valid professional resume showcasing over 5 years of total HR experience in Malaysia. The candidate demonstrates comprehensive experience across the full employee lifecycle, onboarding, payroll support, and HR compliance. Because the provided job description contains minimal criteria, overall match is evaluated based on general HR competency and professional presentation.','Diploma in Human Resource Management — Universiti Teknologi MARA (2018)','HR Executive at Cempaka Business Solutions (2021–Present) and HR Assistant at Melur Retail Group (2019–2021), totaling over 5 years in HR operations.','[\"Full Employee Lifecycle Administration\",\"Recruitment Coordination\",\"Malaysian Employment Law\",\"PDPA Compliance\",\"BrioHR\"]','[\"Has strong operational experience supporting the full employee lifecycle for 180 staff members.\",\"Holds a relevant CIPD Level 3 Foundation Certificate in People Practice alongside a Diploma in HRM.\",\"Demonstrates solid working knowledge of local labor legislation including the Malaysian Employment Act 1955 and PDPA.\"]','[\"The job description lacks detailed functional requirements to confirm specialized software or leadership needs.\",\"Does not hold a bachelor\'s degree in Human Resources or Business Administration.\"]','Hire','Aisyah presents a clean, well-structured HR profile with strong operational and compliance capabilities in Malaysia. S