 and facilities coordination for a 90-person office.\n Organise the firm\'s annual client appreciation event and internal staff celebrations.\n Occasionally assist the 2-person HR team with filing new-hire paperwork and updating personnel files during busy\nperiods.\nFront Desk & Admin Assistant — Teratai Hospitality Group\nKuala Lumpur, MY  | Jul 2016 – Jan 2019\n Handled front-desk operations, correspondence, and basic filing for a 30-person corporate office.\nEDUCATION\nDiploma in Office Management — Kolej Poly-Tech MARA, 2016','Review','Do Not Hire',22,20,20,30,'The uploaded document is a legitimate resume, but the candidate\'s professional background is centered on general office administration rather than human resources. Her HR exposure is limited to occasional support tasks like filing new-hire paperwork, which falls far short of the recruitment, payroll, employee relations, and HR compliance responsibilities outlined in the job description. There is no evidence of proven HR role experience, HR systems proficiency, or knowledge of Malaysian employment law. Overall alignment with the core requirements of this HR Executive position is very weak.','Diploma in Office Management from Kolej Poly-Tech MARA, 2016. No HR-specific or professional HR certification (such as CIPD or SHRM) is listed.','5 years as an Administrative Executive handling office operations, vendor coordination, and event planning, plus prior front desk/admin experience; HR involvement is limited to occasional filing support for a 2-person HR team.','[\"Office Administration\",\"Vendor & Facilities Coordination\",\"Event Planning\",\"Filing & Documentation\",\"Microsoft Office (advanced Excel)\"]','[\"Has experience organising company events and internal celebrations, which aligns with the JD\'s request for employee engagement activity support.\",\"Proficient in Microsoft Office, meeting one of the baseline technical requirements.\",\"Has some exposure to HR filing and personnel record updates, showing basic familiarity with HR documentation.\",\"Demonstrates strong administrative and organisational skills that could transfer to HR administrative support tasks.\"]','[\"Resume explicitly states no dedicated recruitment, payroll, or employee-relations experience, which are core pillars of this role.\",\"No mention of any HR management systems or HRIS proficiency despite this being a listed requirement.\",\"No professional HR qualification such as CIPD or SHRM, and no evidence of knowledge in Malaysian employment law.\",\"No experience conducting interviews, coordinating hiring processes, or supporting HR compliance activities as required by the job description.\"]','Do Not Hire','Michelle\'s background is strongly administrative rather than HR-focused, and her resume self-identifies clear gaps in recruitment, payroll, and employee relations experience central to this role. She does not meet the proven HR role experience requirement and lacks any HR systems or employment law knowledge. She is not a suitable fit for this HR Executive position based on current qualifications.','1. Can you describe any hands-on experience you have had with recruitment, payroll processing, or handling employee relations issues? 2. Are you familiar with any HR management systems or Malaysian employment legislation, and if so, can you provide specific examples?',1,'2026-08-21 03:30:10',30,'uploads/6a87c63736aa3_3_MAYBE_Michelle_Wong.pdf','https://www.youtube.com/',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-08-21 03:30:10','None',NULL,NULL,NULL),('app_c020e11a',18,'Test 4',NULL,NULL,'5_DO_NOT_HIRE_not_a_resume_recipe.pdf','Grandma Bea\'s Weekend Banana Bread\nIngredients: 3 ripe bananas, 1/3 cup melted butter, 3/4 cup sugar, 1 egg (beaten), 1 teaspoon vanilla\nextract, 1 teaspoon baking soda, pinch of salt, 1 1/2 cups all-purpose flour.\nInstructions: Preheat the oven to 350F (175C) and lightly grease a loaf pan. In a large bowl, mash the\nbananas with a fork until smooth. Mix in the melted butter, then the sugar, egg, and vanilla. Sprinkle\nthe baking soda and salt over the mixture and stir in. Add the flour last and mix until just combined; do\nnot overmix. Pour the batter into the prepared loaf pan and bake for 55-60 minutes, or until a\ntoothpick inserted in the center comes out clean. Let cool in the pan for 10 minutes before turning out\nonto a wire rack.\nNotes: For a richer flavor, swap half the butter for browned butter. Add a handful of walnuts or\nchocolate chips if desired. Store covered at room temperature for up to 3 days.','Grandma Bea\'s Weekend Banana Bread\nIngredients: 3 ripe bananas, 1/3 cup melted butter, 3/4 cup sugar, 1 egg (beaten), 1 teaspoon vanilla\nextract, 1 teaspoon baking soda, pinch of salt, 1 1/2 cups all-purpose flour.\nInstructions: Preheat the oven to 350F (175C) and lightly grease a loaf pan. In a large bowl, mash the\nbananas with a fork until smooth. Mix in the melted butter, then the sugar, egg, and vanilla. Sprinkle\nthe baking soda and salt over the mixture and stir in. Add the flour last and mix until just combined; do\nnot overmix. Pour the batter into the prepared loaf pan and bake for 55-60 minutes, or until a\ntoothpick inserted in the center comes out clean. Let cool in the pan for 10 minutes before turning out\nonto a wire rack.\nNotes: For a richer flavor, swap half the butter for browned butter. Add a handful of walnuts or\nchocolate chips if desired. Store covered at room temperature for up to 3 days.','Review','Do Not Hire',0,0,0,0,'INVALID DOCUMENT REJECTED BY ATS: The uploaded file does not contain a standard candidate resume structure, work experience, or professional qualifications.','None / Not Provided','None / Not Provided','[\"Invalid Document Format\"]','[\"None - Invalid Document Format\"]','[\"Uploaded document is not a valid candidate resume\\/CV [Resume Evidence: \\\"Grandma Bea\'s Weekend Banana Bread Ingredients: 3 ripe bananas, 1\\/3 cup melted butter, 3\\/4 cup sugar...\\\"]\",\"Fails mandatory ATS parsing and qualification standards.\"]','Do Not Hire','Automatically rejected by ATS screening due to non-resume file content.','1. Please submit an official professional CV/Resume.\n2. Why was a non-resume document uploaded for this position?',1,'2026-08-20 08:26:21',19,'uploads/6a86ba2b7d308_5_DO_NOT_HIRE_not_a_resume_recipe.pdf','https://www.youtube.com/',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-08-20 08:26:21','None',NULL,NULL,NULL),('app_c51a1cb5',23,'Test 5',NULL,NULL,'6a97e6f1e755b_1_STRONG_HIRE_Aisyah_Rahman.pdf','Aisyah Rahman\nHR Executive\nPetaling Jaya, Selangor, MY  | +60 12 345 6721  | aisyah.rahman@fictionalmail.com  | \nlinkedin.com/in/aisyahrahman-demo\nSUMMARY\nHR Executive with 4 years of hands-on experience supporting the full employee lifecycle for a mid-sized services\ncompany in Malaysia. Comfortable managing recruitment coordination, onboarding, training logistics, HR records,\npayroll administration support, and employee relations with discretion and professionalism. Solid working knowledge\nof the Malaysian Employment Act 1955 and PDPA requirements.\nSKILLS\nFull Employee Lifecycle Administration  | Recruitment Coordination & Preliminary Interviews  | Onboarding &\nOffboarding  | Training & Development Coordination  | HR Records & PDPA Compliance  | Payroll Administration\nSupport  | Malaysian Employment Law  | HRMS (BrioHR)  | Microsoft Office (Excel, Word, PowerPoint)  | Employee\nRelations  | Event & Engagement Coordination\nEXPERIENCE\nHR Executive — Cempaka Business Solutions Sdn. Bhd.\nPetaling Jaya, Selangor  | Mar 2021 – Present\n Support the full employee lifecycle for a 180-staff organisation, including recruitment, onboarding, training\ncoordination, and offboarding.\n Draft job descriptions and job postings, and conduct preliminary phone/in-person interviews before shortlisting\ncandidates to hiring managers.\n Maintain employee records in BrioHR and ensure filing practices comply with PDPA requirements.\n Coordinate monthly training sessions and quarterly team-building/engagement events for the company.\n Assist the Finance team with payroll administration, verifying attendance, leave, and claims data each month for\n180 employees.\n Handle day-to-day employee queries on leave, benefits, and HR policy with empathy and confidentiality.\n Support HR compliance reviews to ensure adherence to the Employment Act 1955 and related regulations.\nHR Assistant — Melur Retail Group\nShah Alam, Selangor  | Jan 2019 – Feb 2021\n Provided administrative support to a 3-person HR team, including maintaining HR databases and physical filing\nsystems.\n Assisted with recruitment logistics — scheduling interviews, preparing offer letters, and coordinating new-hire\npaperwork.\nEDUCATION\nDiploma in Human Resource Management — Universiti Teknologi MARA (UiTM), 2018\nSijil Pelajaran Malaysia (SPM) — SMK Bukit Bintang, 2015\nCERTIFICATIONS\nCIPD Level 3 Foundation Certificate in People Practice','Aisyah Rahman\nHR Executive\nPetaling Jaya, Selangor, MY  | +60 12 345 6721  | [REDACTED EMAIL]  | \nlinkedin.com/in/aisyahrahman-demo\nSUMMARY\nHR Executive with 4 years of hands-on experience supporting the full employee lifecycle for a mid-sized services\ncompany in Malaysia. Comfortable managing recruitment coordination, onboarding, training logistics, HR records,\npayroll administration support, and employee relations with discretion and professionalism. Solid working knowledge\nof the Malaysian Employment Act 1955 and PDPA requirements.\nSKILLS\nFull Employee Lifecycle Administration  | Recruitment Coordination & Preliminary Interviews  | Onboarding &\nOffboarding  | Training & Development Coordination  | HR Records & PDPA Compliance  | Payroll Administration\nSupport  | Malaysian Employment Law  | HRMS (BrioHR)  | Microsoft Office (Excel, Word, PowerPoint)  | Employee\nRelations  | Event & Engagement Coordination\nEXPERIENCE\nHR Executive — Cempaka Business Solutions Sdn. Bhd.\nPetaling Jaya, Selangor  | Mar 2021 – Present\n Support the full employee lifecycle for a 180-staff organisation, including recruitment, onboarding, training\ncoordination, and offboarding.\n Draft job descriptions and job postings, and conduct preliminary phone/in-person interviews before shortlisting\ncandidates to hiring managers.\n Maintain employee records in BrioHR and ensure filing practices comply with PDPA requirements.\n Coordinate monthly training sessions and quarterly team-building/engagement events for the company.\n Assist the Finance team with payroll administration, verifying attendance, leave, and claims data each month for\n180 employees.\n Handle day-to-day employee queries on leave, benefits, and HR policy with empathy and confidentiality.\n Support HR compliance reviews to ensure adherence to the Employment Act 1955 and related regulations.\nHR Assistant — Melur Retail Group\nShah Alam, Selangor  | Jan 2019 – Feb 2021\n Provided administrative support to a 3-person HR team, including maintaining HR databases and physical filing\nsystems.\n Assisted with recruitment logistics — scheduling interviews, preparing offer letters, and coordinating new-hire\npaperwork.\nEDUCATION\nDiploma in Human Resource Management — Universiti Teknologi MARA (UiTM), 2018\nSijil Pelajaran Malaysia (SPM) — SMK Bukit Bintang, 2015\nCERTIFICATIONS\nCIPD Level 3 Foundation Certificate in People Practice','Review','Do Not Hire',10,0,5,20,'The candidate submitted a valid professional resume; however, her background is entirely focused on Human Resource Management. She lacks the technical expertise, networking certifications, and engineering experience required for the Network Engineer role. Consequently, there is virtually zero alignment with the core responsibilities outlined in the job description.','Diploma in Human Resource Management — Universiti Teknologi MARA (UiTM)','HR Executive at Cempaka Business Solutions Sdn. Bhd. and HR Assistant at Melur Retail Group (Total ~4 years in HR)','[\"Full Employee Lifecycle Administration\",\"Recruitment Coordination\",\"PDPA Compliance\",\"HRMS (BrioHR)\",\"Microsoft Office\"]','[\"Has a solid professional administrative background with four years of continuous work experience.\",\"Demonstrates strong organizational, coordination, and record-keeping skills.\",\"Proficient in standard workplace software applications such as Microsoft Excel, Word, and PowerPoint.\"]','[\"No documented experience or technical background in network engineering, IT infrastructure, or networking protocols.\",\"Lacks hands-on skills required for network design, implementation, maintenance, and security.\",\"Academic qualifications and certifications are exclusively focused on human resource management rather than IT or Computer Science.\"]','Do Not Hire','The candidate\'s profile represents a complete domain mismatch for a Network Engineer position. She has a dedicated career in HR administration and lacks any relevant network engineering capabilities or qualifications.','1. Do you have any unlisted technical certifications or hands-on experience related to computer networking and IT infrastructure management?\n2. Are you looking to transition from Human Resources into Information Technology, and what relevant technical training have you undertaken?',1,'2026-09-11 03:18:44',20,'uploads/resumes/6a97e6f1e755b_1_STRONG_HIRE_Aisyah_Rahman.pdf',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-09-11 03:18:44','None',NULL,NULL,NULL),('app_d212918b',20,'Test 10',NULL,NULL,'5_DO_NOT_HIRE_not_a_resume_pantry_guide.pdf','Simple Guide to Organising a Home Pantry\nStep 1: Empty the pantry completely and wipe down every shelf with a damp cloth. Check expiry\ndates on all items and discard anything that has gone bad.\nStep 2: Group similar items together — grains and pasta, canned goods, baking supplies, snacks,\nand spices. Clear, airtight containers work best for dry goods like rice, flour, and sugar since they\nkeep pests out and let you see at a glance when you\'re running low.\nStep 3: Store frequently used items at eye level and place heavier or rarely used items on the bottom\nor top shelves. Use small baskets or bins for loose packets so they don\'t get lost at the back.\nStep 4: Label each container and shelf so everyone in the household can find and return items to the\nright place. A simple printed label or masking tape and marker works fine.\nStep 5: Do a quick 10-minute tidy-up once a week and a full restock check once a month, noting\ndown anything that needs to be added to the next grocery list.','Simple Guide to Organising a Home Pantry\nStep 1: Empty the pantry completely and wipe down every shelf with a damp cloth. Check expiry\ndates on all items and discard anything that has gone bad.\nStep 2: Group similar items together — grains and pasta, canned goods, baking supplies, snacks,\nand spices. Clear, airtight containers work best for dry goods like rice, flour, and sugar since they\nkeep pests out and let you see at a glance when you\'re running low.\nStep 3: Store frequently used items at eye level and place heavier or rarely used items on the bottom\nor top shelves. Use small baskets or bins for loose packets so they don\'t get lost at the back.\nStep 4: Label each container and shelf so everyone in the household can find and return items to the\nright place. A simple printed label or masking tape and marker works fine.\nStep 5: Do a quick 10-minute tidy-up once a week and a full restock check once a month, noting\ndown anything that needs to be added to the next grocery list.','Review','Do Not Hire',0,0,0,0,'INVALID DOCUMENT REJECTED BY ATS: The uploaded file does not contain a standard candidate resume structure, work experience, or professional qualifications.','None / Not Provided','None / Not Provided','[\"Invalid Document Format\"]','[\"None - Invalid Document Format\"]','[\"Uploaded document is not a valid candidate resume\\/CV [Resume Evidence: \\\"Simple Guide to Organising a Home Pantry Step 1: Empty the pantry completely and wipe down every she...\\\"]\",\"Fails mandatory ATS parsing and qualification standards.\"]','Do Not Hire','Automatically rejected by ATS screening due to non-resume file content.','1. Please submit an official professional CV/Resume.\n2. Why was a non-resume document uploaded for this position?',1,'2026-08-21 01:46:56',37,'uploads/6a87ae0e60fa8_5_DO_NOT_HIRE_not_a_resume_pantry_guide.pdf','https://www.youtube.com/',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-08-21 01:51:36','None',NULL,NULL,NULL),('app_d3f8e182',20,'testing',NULL,NULL,'HireLah Strategic Revamp & Growth Deck.pdf','','','Review','Do Not Hire',0,0,0,0,'INVALID DOCUMENT REJECTED BY ATS: The uploaded file does not contain a standard candidate resume structure or relevant professional experience.','Not provided','Not provided','[]','[\"None - Invalid Document Format\"]','[\"Uploaded document is not a valid resume\\/CV.\",\"Fails mandatory ATS parsing standards.\"]','Do Not Hire','Automatically rejected by ATS screening due to non-resume file content.','1. Please submit an official professional CV/Resume.\n2. Why was a non-resume document uploaded for this position?',1,'2026-09-02 06:21:55',14,'uploads/6a97c07c62a81_HireLah Strategic Revamp & Growth Deck.pdf','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0_6AK52kSVQ',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-09-02 06:21:55','None',NULL,NULL,NULL),('app_d8e918b0',14,'zul ariffin',NULL,NULL,'sample-local-pdf.pdf','1 \nSample PDF \n \nCreated for testing PDFObject \n \nThis PDF is three pages long. Three long pages. Or three short pages if \nyou’re optimistic. Is it the same as saying “three long minutes”, knowing \nthat all minutes are the same duration, and one cannot possibly be longer \nthan the other? If these pages are all the same size, can one possibly be \nlonger than the other? \n \nI digress. Here’s some Latin. Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet, consectetur adipiscing elit. Integer nec \nodio. Praesent libero. Sed cursus ante dapibus diam. Sed nisi. Nulla quis sem at nibh elementum \nimperdie