INSERT INTO `resume_reviews` VALUES (1,37,'4_DO_NOT_HIRE_Kevin_Lim_field_mismatch.pdf','Kevin Lim Wei Jian\nJunior Graphic Designer\nPenang, MY  | +60 16 552 3390  | kevin.lim@fictionalmail.com  | linkedin.com/in/kevinlim-demo\nSUMMARY\nJunior graphic designer with 3 years of experience creating marketing visuals, packaging artwork, and social media\ngraphics for a consumer products company. No experience in human resources, recruitment, payroll, or office\nadministration.\nSKILLS\nAdobe Photoshop  | Adobe Illustrator  | Figma  | Packaging Design  | Social Media Graphics  | Brand Visual Identity  | \nPrint Production Coordination\nEXPERIENCE\nJunior Graphic Designer — Warna Kreatif Studio\nGeorgetown, Penang  | Apr 2022 – Present\n Design packaging artwork and marketing collateral for consumer product clients.\n Create social media graphics and short animated ads for client campaigns.\nDesign Intern — Pixel Bay Advertising\nGeorgetown, Penang  | Jan 2021 – Mar 2022\n Supported senior designers on print production files and client mockups.\nEDUCATION\nDiploma in Graphic Design — Dasein Academy of Art, 2021','Kevin Lim Wei Jian\nJunior Graphic Designer\nPenang, MY  | +60 16 552 3390  | [REDACTED EMAIL]  | linkedin.com/in/kevinlim-demo\nSUMMARY\nJunior graphic designer with 3 years of experience creating marketing visuals, packaging artwork, and social media\ngraphics for a consumer products company. No experience in human resources, recruitment, payroll, or office\nadministration.\nSKILLS\nAdobe Photoshop  | Adobe Illustrator  | Figma  | Packaging Design  | Social Media Graphics  | Brand Visual Identity  | \nPrint Production Coordination\nEXPERIENCE\nJunior Graphic Designer — Warna Kreatif Studio\nGeorgetown, Penang  | Apr 2022 – Present\n Design packaging artwork and marketing collateral for consumer product clients.\n Create social media graphics and short animated ads for client campaigns.\nDesign Intern — Pixel Bay Advertising\nGeorgetown, Penang  | Jan 2021 – Mar 2022\n Supported senior designers on print production files and client mockups.\nEDUCATION\nDiploma in Graphic Design — Dasein Academy of Art, 2021',71,'Needs Some Work','Automated check (AI screening not configured): this resume contains standard sections and 124 words. A few areas below would make it stronger.','[\"Contact details are present and easy to find.\",\"Includes a summary\\/profile section that frames your experience up front.\",\"Uses numbers and measurable results to back up claims, which stands out to recruiters.\"]','[\"Resume looks quite short \\u2014 consider expanding on your responsibilities and achievements in each role.\"]','Automated check only — for detailed formatting feedback (layout, spacing, section order), AI screening needs to be configured by an administrator.','[\"Use standard section headings like \\\"Experience\\\", \\\"Education\\\", and \\\"Skills\\\" so ATS software can parse them correctly.\",\"Avoid tables, columns, or text boxes for key content \\u2014 some ATS parsers cannot read them.\",\"Save and submit as a text-based PDF, not a scanned image.\"]','2026-08-27 07:49:59'),(2,20,'RESUME NURIMAN HANAFI.pdf','Nuriman Hanafi Bin Kadir \nSOFTWARE ENGINEERING INTERN \n \n \n01116208648 	nuriman.kadir01@s.unikl.edu.my 11-4 Apartment Melati Impian, \nJalan Madrasah Gombak Setia, \n53100 Kuala Lumpur. \n \nObjective As an intern in the software engineering field, my main goal is to aid in creating and \ndelivering strong software applications through good coding practices, teamwork in \ndesigning systems and effective software performance. My aim is to help create a \nproductive agile team by effective communication, problem-solving and gaining \nknowledge of emerging technologies. I am looking forward for a 4-month IT \ninternship from 3\nrd \nof August until 4\nth \nDecember 2026 to implement my coding and \nproject management skills. \n \nEducation Universiti Kuala Lumpur MIIT \nBachelor of Information Technology (Hons) in Software Engineering \nCGPA 3.48 \n \nUniversiti Kuala Lumpur MIIT \nDiploma in Information Technology \nCGPA 3.30 \n \nExperience Chronological work history and industry exposure: \n \n \nFeb 2024 - June 2024 May 2025 - Oct 2025 	Nov 2025 – July 2026 \n \nAll IT Hypermarket \nPlaza Low Yat (Intern) \nTechnician / Sale Assistant \nDiagnosed and repaired PC hardware \ncomponents as part of software \nengineering knowledge. Assisted \ncustomers with custom system \nconfigurations. \nOH!SOME \nMelawati Mall (Part-time) \nStorekeeper \nManaged floor inventory and \nconducted product velocity analysis \nby working with team members to \nensure smooth operation of daily \nactivities in retail store. \nTudungPeople Sdn Bhd \nStarparc Point (Part-time) \nWarehouse Operator \nOversee day-to-day inventory \nmanagement processes and logistics \ndata collection with a high degree of \naccuracy in high volume environments. \n \n \nLanguages \nTechnologies \nPHP, HTML, ASP, SQL, Java, Python, C++ \nFlutter, Enterprise JavaBeans (EJB), Java Server Pages (JSP), MySQL, Git, Gemini \nAPI \n \n \nProjects CareMind | Lead Developer \nDesigned and developed a responsive dashboard for user support using PHP, \nHTML, JS and MySQL database connection. Implemented Large Language Model \nAPIs (Gemini API) for real-time assistance through AI technology.\n\nMIIT-Hire Marketplace System | System Architect & Developer \nDesigned system architecture diagrams and use cases. Developed backend \nfunctionality using Java (Enterprise JavaBeans and JavaServer Pages). \n \nCore Competencies Proficient in Object Oriented Programming (OOP), Relational Database design, and \nMobile Application Architecture. \nExperienced in creating responsive interfaces, writing high-quality reusable code, \nand incorporating third party APIs into existing frameworks. \n \nCoursework Academic Focus: Object-Oriented Programming, Database Systems \nManagement, Web Applications, Mobile Applications, System Architecture & \nDesign, and Artificial Intelligence Integration. \n \nReferences Azaliza Zainal - Ts. Dr. \nAcademic Advisor in Univesiti Kuala Lumpur \nazaliza@unikl.edu.my','Nuriman Hanafi Bin Kadir \nSOFTWARE ENGINEERING INTERN \n \n \n[REDACTED PHONE] 	[REDACTED EMAIL] 11-4 Apartment Melati Impian, \nJalan Madrasah Gombak Setia, \n53100 Kuala Lumpur. \n \nObjective As an intern in the software engineering field, my main goal is to aid in creating and \ndelivering strong software applications through good coding practices, teamwork in \ndesigning systems and effective software performance. My aim is to help create a \nproductive agile team by effective communication, problem-solving and gaining \nknowledge of emerging technologies. I am looking forward for a 4-month IT \ninternship from 3\nrd \nof August until 4\nth \nDecember 2026 to implement my coding and \nproject management skills. \n \nEducation Universiti Kuala Lumpur MIIT \nBachelor of Information Technology (Hons) in Software Engineering \nCGPA 3.48 \n \nUniversiti Kuala Lumpur MIIT \nDiploma in Information Technology \nCGPA 3.30 \n \nExperience Chronological work history and industry exposure: \n \n \nFeb 2024 - June 2024 May 2025 - Oct 2025 	Nov 2025 – July 2026 \n \nAll IT Hypermarket \nPlaza Low Yat (Intern) \nTechnician / Sale Assistant \nDiagnosed and repaired PC hardware \ncomponents as part of software \nengineering knowledge. Assisted \ncustomers with custom system \nconfigurations. \nOH!SOME \nMelawati Mall (Part-time) \nStorekeeper \nManaged floor inventory and \nconducted product velocity analysis \nby working with team members to \nensure smooth operation of daily \nactivities in retail store. \nTudungPeople Sdn Bhd \nStarparc Point (Part-time) \nWarehouse Operator \nOversee day-to-day inventory \nmanagement processes and logistics \ndata collection with a high degree of \naccuracy in high volume environments. \n \n \nLanguages \nTechnologies \nPHP, HTML, ASP, SQL, Java, Python, C++ \nFlutter, Enterprise JavaBeans (EJB), Java Server Pages (JSP), MySQL, Git, Gemini \nAPI \n \n \nProjects CareMind | Lead Developer \nDesigned and developed a responsive dashboard for user support using PHP, \nHTML, JS and MySQL database connection. Implemented Large Language Model \nAPIs (Gemini API) for real-time assistance through AI technology.\n\nMIIT-Hire Marketplace System | System Architect & Developer \nDesigned system architecture diagrams and use cases. Developed backend \nfunctionality using Java (Enterprise JavaBeans and JavaServer Pages). \n \nCore Competencies Proficient in Object Oriented Programming (OOP), Relational Database design, and \nMobile Application Architecture. \nExperienced in creating responsive interfaces, writing high-quality reusable code, \nand incorporating third party APIs into existing frameworks. \n \nCoursework Academic Focus: Object-Oriented Programming, Database Systems \nManagement, Web Applications, Mobile Applications, System Architecture & \nDesign, and Artificial Intelligence Integration. \n \nReferences Azaliza Zainal - Ts. Dr. \nAcademic Advisor in Univesiti Kuala Lumpur \n[REDACTED EMAIL]',68,'Good','You have a solid academic background with a strong CGPA and impressive hands-on project experience using modern technologies like the Gemini API, Java, and Flutter. However, the current layout uses side-by-side columns for work experience, which creates severe parsing issues in Applicant Tracking Systems. By moving to a single-column format, quantifying your achievements, and polishing verb tenses, your resume will be in great shape for internship applications.','[\"Strong academic foundation with a high CGPA in both Bachelor\'s and Diploma programs.\",\"Relevant technical projects showcasing practical application of web, database, and AI integrations (Gemini API).\",\"Clear, comprehensive categorization of technologies, programming languages, and core competencies.\"]','[\"Reformat the work experience section from a side-by-side layout into a standard vertical, chronological list.\",\"Add measurable metrics and outcomes to your project and work descriptions (e.g., user count, resolution rates, performance gains).\",\"Fix verb tense inconsistencies in past roles (e.g., change \'Oversee\' to \'Oversewed\' or \'Managed\').\",\"Streamline the objective section to focus on your core skills and value, moving specific availability dates to your cover letter or application form.\"]','The multi-column layout used in the experience section will cause ATS software to read lines horizontally across different jobs, scrambling your job titles, dates, and descriptions. Reorganize all sections into a standard single-column design.','[\"Avoid multi-column tables or side-by-side boxes; ATS parsers scan from top-to-bottom, left-to-right, and will mix up text across columns.\",\"Remove the \'References\' section to save space, as references are typically requested separately during later interview stages.\",\"Ensure section headings remain simple and standard (e.g., \'Work Experience\' instead of \'Experience Chronological work history...\').\"]','2026-09-08 03:25:03'),(3,20,'AMIRUL FARIS RESUME.pdf','EDUCATION\nSUMMARY\nPROJECTS\nTRAINING AND CERTIFICATION\nMarch 2021-October 2023KOLEJ PROFESIONAL MARA BERANANG\nDiploma in Computer Science\nCGPA: 3.62\nMarch 2024-PresentUNIVERSITY KUALA LUMPUR MALAYSIAN INSTITUTE OF INFORMATION\nTECHNOLOGY (MIIT)\nBachelor of Information Technology (Hons.) in Software Engineering \nCGPA: 3.31\nSoftware Engineering undergraduate at UniKL MIIT with a 3.31 CGPA. Skilled in web development,\ndatabase management, AI integration, and software engineering principles. Experienced in developing\napplications using PHP, Laravel, JavaScript, HTML, CSS, SQL, and Google Cloud Firestore, alongside\nGenerative AI integration via the Google Gemini API. Actively seeking a Software Engineer internship from\nOctober 2026 to March 2027 to leverage technical expertise and drive impactful software solutions.\nAMIRUL FARIS BIN SUHAIMINSemarak, 54100, Kuala Lumpur |016-6034329 | amirulfaris077@gmail.com |linkedin.com/in/amirulfarisuhaimin \nATTENDANCE TRACKING SYSTEM FOR DOREMI SERVICES& RENTAL SDN. BHD.\nCo-developed an end-to-end HR attendance management solution with a two-person team,\ncomprising a web-based administrative portal and a partner-built mobile application.\nLed design and development of the web portal and backend architecture in PHP and Laravel, building\na responsive interface with JavaScript, HTML, and CSS.\nEngineered a hybrid database architecture combining SQL and Google Cloud Firestore (NoSQL) to\nsupport real-time data synchronization with the mobile application.\nIntegrated the Google Gemini API for Generative AI features, automating data processing tasks such\nas AI-assisted overtime verification.\nImplemented automated PDF report generation with DomPDF for attendance and administrative\nrecords.\nTechnologies Used: PHP, Laravel Framework, JavaScript, HTML, CSS, SQL, Google Cloud Firestore,\nGoogle Gemini API, DomPDF, Generative AI Integration (Google Gemini API)\nGoogle Project Management Professional Certificate — core project management principles,\nstrategic planning, and Agile methodologies.\nDevSecOps Foundation Certification — Demonstrated understanding of secure software\ndevelopment, bridging the gap between development, IT operations, and security to ensure safe and\nefficient system deployments.\n\nADDITIONAL INFORMATION\nTechnical Skills: PHP, Laravel, Python, JavaScript, HTML, CSS, SQL, Google Cloud Firestore\n(NoSQL), Generative AI Integration (Google Gemini API), Web Prototyping, Database\nManagement, Front-End Development, Back-End Development\nMethodologies: Agile, IT Project Management, System Documentation, Software Engineering\nPrinciples\nSoft Skills: Customer Service, Interpersonal Communication, Team Collaboration, Problem-\nSolving, Adaptability, Sales and Promotion, Mobilegraphy\nLanguages: English, Malay\nWORK EXPERIENCE\nFeb 2026Event Promoter, The Aromania by Fragrance Festival Malaysia\nRepresented JOYRIA Beauty and GALAXY perfume brands at the Malaysia Muslim Festival, effectively\ncommunicating unique fragrance notes and profiles to visitors.\nEducated customers in discovering suitable scents by providing expert advice, demonstrating\nproducts, and tailoring personalized recommendations.\nMaximized high foot traffic in a fast-paced festival setting to actively engage potential buyers and\ngenerate promotional sales.\nJul 2024 - Oct 2024Retail Assistant, ZTE Mobile \nAdvised customers through product selections by leveraging expert-level knowledge of mobile\ndevices, consistently surpassing sales targets.\nProcessed efficient sales transactions, addressed customer inquiries, and accelerated overall store\nrevenue growth.\nCoordinated store visual merchandising standards and streamlined inventory management to ensure\noptimal product availability.\nAug 2023 - Jan 2024System Engineering Intern, Bastion Solution Sdn Bhd | Intern \nAdministered and optimized the government DDMS 2.0 system, ensuring high availability and\nseamless daily operations for end-users.\nExecuted continuous server monitoring to identify and proactively mitigate potential technical\ndisruptions.\nTroubleshot and resolved user-reported technical issues efficiently, providing vital support and\nelevating overall system satisfaction.\nREFERENCES INDUSTRIAL LINKAGES (IL)\nTs.Nurdatillah Hasim\nnurdatillah@unikl.edu.my \n(+60)17-5636371 \nNoor Suzieany Binti M Radzali\nnoorsuzieany@unikl.edu.my \n(+60)12-3664184\nLEADERSHIP & EXTRACURRICULAR ACTIVITIES\nLeader Team, TECHNOPRENEURSHIP \nTreasurer, Phantom Runners Club (PRC)\nMember, CREATIVE MULTIMEDIA CLUB\nMember, NETBALL CLUB\nMember, UniKL MIIT NETSYS CLUB\nParticipate Efootball Unikl E-Sport Carnival (UESC) 2025\nProfessional & Student Organizations\nRunner, Half Marathoner\nSports','EDUCATION\nSUMMARY\nPROJECTS\nTRAINING AND CERTIFICATION\nMarch 2021-October 2023KOLEJ PROFESIONAL MARA BERANANG\nDiploma in Computer Science\nCGPA: 3.62\nMarch 2024-PresentUNIVERSITY KUALA LUMPUR MALAYSIAN INSTITUTE OF INFORMATION\nTECHNOLOGY (MIIT)\nBachelor of Information Technology (Hons.) in Software Engineering \nCGPA: 3.31\nSoftware Engineering undergraduate at UniKL MIIT with a 3.31 CGPA. Skilled in web development,\ndatabase management, AI integration, and software engineering principles. Experienced in developing\napplications using PHP, Laravel, JavaScript, HTML, CSS, SQL, and Google Cloud Firestore, alongside\nGenerative AI integration via the Google Gemini API. Actively seeking a Software Engineer internship from\nOctober 2026 to March 2027 to leverage technical expertise and drive impactful software solutions.\nAMIRUL FARIS BIN SUHAIMINSemarak, 54100, Kuala Lumpur |[REDACTED PHONE] | [REDACTED EMAIL] |linkedin.com/in/amirulfarisuhaimin \nATTENDANCE TRACKING SYSTEM FOR DOREMI SERVICES& RENTAL SDN. BHD.\nCo-developed an end-to-end HR attendance management solution with a two-person team,\ncomprising a web-based administrative portal and a partner-built mobile application.\nLed design and development of the web portal and backend architecture in PHP and Laravel, building\na responsive interface with JavaScript, HTML, and CSS.\nEngineered a hybrid database architecture combining SQL and Google Cloud Firestore (NoSQL) to\nsupport real-time data synchronization with the mobile application.\nIntegrated the Google Gemini API for Generative AI features, automating data processing tasks such\nas AI-assisted overtime verification.\nImplemented automated PDF report generation with DomPDF for attendance and administrative\nrecords.\nTechnologies Used: PHP, Laravel Framework, JavaScript, HTML, CSS, SQL, Google Cloud Firestore,\nGoogle Gemini API, DomPDF, Generative AI Integration (Google Gemini API)\nGoogle Project Management Professional Certificate — core project management principles,\nstrategic planning, and Agile methodologies.\nDevSecOps Foundation Certification — Demonstrated understanding of secure software\ndevelopment, bridging the gap between development, IT operations, and security to ensure safe and\nefficient system deployments.\n\nADDITIONAL INFORMATION\nTechnical Skills: PHP, Laravel, Python, JavaScript, HTML, CSS, SQL, Google Cloud Firestore\n(NoSQL), Generative AI Integration (Google Gemini API), Web Prototyping, Database\nManagement, Front-End Development, Back-End Development\nMethodologies: Agile, IT Project Management, System Documentation, Software Engineering\nPrinciples\nSoft Skills: Customer Service, Interpersonal Communication, Team Collaboration, Problem-\nSolving, Adaptability, Sales and Promotion, Mobilegraphy\nLanguages: English, Malay\nWORK EXPERIENCE\nFeb 2026Event Promoter, The Aromania by Fragrance Festival Malaysia\nRepresented JOYRIA Beauty and GALAXY perfume brands at the Malaysia Muslim Festival, effectively\ncommunicating unique fragrance notes and profiles to visitors.\nEducated customers in discovering suitable scents by providing expert advice, demonstrating\nproducts, and tailoring personalized recommendations.\nMaximized high foot traffic in a fast-paced festival setting to actively engage potential buyers and\ngenerate promotional sales.\nJul 2024 - Oct 2024Retail Assistant, ZTE Mobile \nAdvised customers through product selections by leveraging expert-level knowledge of mobile\ndevices, consistently surpassing sales targets.\nProcessed efficient sales transactions, addressed customer inquiries, and accelerated overall store\nrevenue growth.\nCoordinated store visual merchandising standards and streamlined inventory management to ensure\noptimal product availability.\nAug 2023 - Jan 2024System Engineering Intern, Bastion Solution Sdn Bhd | Intern \nAdministered and optimized the government DDMS 2.0 system, ensuring high availability and\nseamless daily operations for end-users.\nExecuted continuous server monitoring to identify and proactively mitigate potential technical\ndisruptions.\nTroubleshot and resolved user-reported technical issues efficiently, providing vital support and\nelevating overall system satisfaction.\nREFERENCES INDUSTRIAL LINKAGES (IL)\nTs.Nurdatillah Hasim\n[REDACTED EMAIL] \n(+60)17-5636371 \nNoor Suzieany Binti M Radzali\n[REDACTED EMAIL] \n(+60)12-3664184\nLEADERSHIP & EXTRACURRICULAR ACTIVITIES\nLeader Team, TECHNOPRENEURSHIP \nTreasurer, Phantom Runners Club (PRC)\nMember, CREATIVE MULTIMEDIA CLUB\nMember, NETBALL CLUB\nMember, UniKL MIIT NETSYS CLUB\nParticipate Efootball Unikl E-Sport Carnival (UESC) 2025\nProfessional & Student Organizations\nRunner, Half Marathoner\nSports',76,'Good','You have a solid technical background with relevant software engineering education, an impressive full-stack project, and valuable industry certifications like DevSecOps and Google Project Management. However, your resume\'s visual layout appears to be causing structural scrambling during automated parsing, suggesting complex formatting like columns or text boxes. Additionally, your work experience bullet points focus heavily on duties rather than measurable achievements and hard metrics.','[\"Strong technical project description showcasing modern full-stack skills, hybrid database architecture, and Google Gemini API integration.\",\"Valuable industry certifications (DevSecOps Foundation and Google PM Professional) that highlight initiative beyond standard coursework.\",\"Clear alignment with targeted software engineering roles through a well-defined objective and clear technical stack.\"]','[\"Quantify your experience and achievements with concrete metrics (e.g., number of system tickets resolved, performance optimization percentages, or sales volume exceeded).\",\"Reformat the resume into a single-column layout so ATS parsers do not scramble section titles, dates, and header content.\",\"Refine the Soft Skills list to remove non-standard or irrelevant entries for software engineering roles, such as \'Mobilegraphy\'.\",\"Verify date accuracy across your document, particularly the \'Feb 2026\' event promoter entry which reflects a future date.\",\"Remove personal references from the main resume layout to free up space for more detailed project accomplishments.\"]','The extracted text shows stacked section headers at the top and disjointed text elements at the bottom, which is a classic symptom of multi-column templates or text boxes breaking under ATS extraction. Rebuilding your document using standard single-column formatting will immediately resolve this.','[\"Use standard, single-column layouts created in basic word processors without using text boxes or table grids.\",\"Ensure standard headers like \'Work Experience\', \'Education\', and \'Projects\' precede their respective contents cleanly.\",\"Avoid adding graphics, icons, or complex sidebar layouts that confuse optical character recognition (OCR) and ATS parsers.\"]','2026-09-14 07:36:47');
